Description: qtquick: Leave the items' moves to Qt Quick while it draws the pair
 .
 The edition's Qt Quick now draws a window whose elements show depth once per
 eye itself: it moves each item by the parallax the item carries, relative to
 what it lies on, and cuts an item deeper than what it lies on to its own
 rectangle, an item that draws itself too. While it does, it says so with the
 window's _q_stereo_pair (Depth::PairProperty). Union then moves no item, so
 nothing moves twice, and keeps only what differs inside an element: the shadow
 left where it falls.
 .
 Both eyes of a frame show the same moment of a motion in depth, the parallax
 the engine reads follows the motion frame by frame, and Union's rectangles and
 icons are aligned to pixels where the engine draws them, so they land on whole
 pixels as they did when Union moved them itself.
